# Mobile-First — Hard Requirement

Visitors reach these businesses on a phone, from a maps listing or a search result. The phone view is the product. Desktop is the secondary case.

## Build order

- Build the mobile layout first, then scale up. Never design desktop and squeeze it down.
- Keep the WOW on mobile. Cap complexity — fewer particles, lower DPR, simpler camera path — but never fall back to a flat static page.

## Verify at every breakpoint

Scroll the full page at 360x800, 390x844, 768x1024, and 1440x900.

- No horizontal overflow at any width
- Body copy at 16px or larger
- Tap targets at least 44x44px with real spacing between them
- `dvh` rather than `vh` for full-height sections, so the mobile URL bar does not clip the hero
- Safe-area insets respected on notched devices

## Performance

- Throttle and check the 3D canvas. Below roughly 30fps, reduce the scene until it holds. A stuttering hero is worse than a simpler one.
- Mobile Lighthouse runs as part of `yarn quality:gate`. A desktop-only pass is not a pass.
